    Smoke fixtures: correct two assertions that no production code satisfies
    
    Two tests failed on canonical main for reasons unrelated to the code under
    test:
    
    - boot-smoke required every launch prompt to contain "Standing Founder
      instruction for every Viche agent launch". That phrase exists only in the
      test; the policy actually injected by sitting.sh is headed "Standing
      Founder operational instructions". Match the real heading, keeping the
      original intent (the reporting policy must reach every prompt).
    
    - innovation-centre-smoke called branch-health.sh, which now treats missing
      or stale monitoring snapshots as its own adverse evidence and therefore
      exits non-zero under `set -e` before the assertions run. Supply fresh
      snapshots, as boot-smoke already does, and a fixture LAWS.md without the
      Executive Innovation Office Act heading.
    
    Both changes are test-only. With them, the whole suite on top of 91a136e
    fails only at tests/ballot-integrity.sh (protected M-024 ballot records).

diff --git a/tests/boot-smoke.sh b/tests/boot-smoke.sh
index 88f49733..93e07766 100644
--- a/tests/boot-smoke.sh
+++ b/tests/boot-smoke.sh
@@ -64,7 +64,7 @@ case "$action" in
             *) exit 6 ;;
         esac
         # Every newly launched Town agent must receive the Founder reporting rule.
-        case "$prompt" in *"Standing Founder instruction for every Viche agent launch"*) :;; *) exit 95;; esac
+        case "$prompt" in *"Standing Founder operational instructions"*) :;; *) exit 95;; esac
         printf '%s\n' "$id" >> "$MOCK_STATE/ran"
         case "$prompt" in *"This is independent executive delivery"*) printf '%s\n' "$id" >> "$MOCK_STATE/executive-ran";; esac
         ;;
diff --git a/tests/innovation-centre-smoke.sh b/tests/innovation-centre-smoke.sh
